idden  details the mysteries of the house seem  to be endless executive producer carlton  hughes explained the challenge of  creating the sets in an interview with  cbr when we adapted it for production we  had to make it really functional and  practical a lot of attention was paid to  the home's layout creating circularities  so that the characters had paths to walk  where the camera could easily follow  them rory cheney was the show's  production designer and according to one  of the show's directors michael morris  he went all out with small details in  the home even down to hiding the kh  initials of keyhouse throughout the  wooden moldings the director refers to  the manor as a puzzle box you can unfold  the show's a mystery so there had to be  plenty of places for things to be hidden  and discovered your house is filled with  amazing keys  while key house may not be entirely real  the well house was really built in the  countryside not far from the home's  exterior set are you my echo  keyhouse's yard was made to look wild  and unruly while filming in canada was  plenty cold the set designers added  details like fake cotton snow which  looks incredibly believable for such a  simple practical set dressing but if you  continue down the path you'll make your  way to the very real wellhouse  of course a lot of attention was paid to  detail here like how the intricate  pattern of the ceilings is identical to  the pattern on the echo key the actors  were able to film their scenes on this  set while cgi was added later to make  things seem more eerie and creepy and to  make the well look bottomless why are  you down there echoes can come to life  in this place you likely noticed that  key house's layout is pretty chaotic the  outside of the home isn't balanced or  symmetrical and inside there's no rhyme  or reason to how the rooms are organized  this was done entirely on purpose  gabriel rodriguez who did the artwork  for the comic book series was trained as  an architect he treated the design of  keyhouse as an architectural challenge  he wanted it to be as uneven and  unsymmetrical as possible from every  point of view he even ended up drawing  architectural blueprints of the house to  make it believable while keyhouse was  supposed to be a bit intimidating  director michael morris wanted to make  sure it wasn't too scary he told decider  that he aimed to make it dilapidated but  not menacing there's a lot of things to  discover throughout the home but he  wanted it to be more inviting than other  haunted horror stories like the haunting  of hill house do you think the house is  scary or just interesting going to a new  school starting in the middle of the  year might suck but also it might not  scenes that took place at the show's  high school matheson academy were filmed  at the humber college lakeshore campus  located on the shores of lake ontario  this college might actually be the  closest to a haunting the show had to  experience in real life the neo-gothic  building is considered to be one of  toronto's most haunted places the  grounds of the college were once home to  an asylum and there have been hundreds  of reports of people seeing apparitions  in or around the college these ghosts  have been especially associated with the  underground tunnels on campus we wonder  if any of the cast experienced something  supernatural while on set i think we're  starting to see how that begins  while most matheson academy scenes were  really filmed in a school the school's  cafeteria wasn't really a cafeteria at  all it's actually the library of an  anglican school in toronto called  wycliffe college the books were removed  and long wooden tables were brought in  for filming the elegant building is  located at the university of toronto's  st george campus the school was founded  in 1877  and we can definitely see the similarity  to schools like cambridge and oxford  which helped inspire other great school  sets like those in harry 