achusetts town in  nova scotia they did the same thing for  the english city they actually just used  stock footage for the first few  establishing shots  but the walk by the river was filmed in  mill race park in cambridge ontario the  other scenes in the english town were  all filmed at springer market square in  kingston ontario so the cast and crew  didn't have to travel too far for their  little english journey with the magical  key  if i do get back that anywhere key  i'm coming straight to nebraska the work  that went into making lock and key  believable yet uniquely imaginative is  incredible especially when you consider  that there were two adaptations in the  works before the netflix series they  never panned out because key house was  just so hard to design so let us know  which of the movie's real life sets  would you want to visit most
 

